  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse finite_original_differential_support directly rather than constructing another canonical divisor. The original uniformizer derivative is already one, so center evaluations need no separate derivative-nonvanishing development. Reuse finite reading linearity instead of introducing a new evaluation linear-map hierarchy. Extract a basis from the actual evaluation vectors and apply the native inverse-function theorem directly to their analytic primitives, avoiding an additional determinant-matrix interface. The existing local Abel-Jacobi identity produces explicit differences of original places with degree zero by the proved residue-field dimension one.",
  "discharged": "Every vector modulo the integer span of actual loop periods is represented by an actual degree-zero original divisor. An injective original chart disk makes the place space infinite. If an original regular differential vanished at every center, exact residue orders would make its differential order positive at every place, contradicting the already proved finite support of nonzero original differentials. These evaluations therefore span the complex coordinate space. Native linear algebra extracts an independent evaluation frame; full-chart primitives give a sum map whose derivative is the corresponding continuous linear equivalence. The native inverse-function theorem puts a neighborhood of zero into the actual image of degree-zero divisors modulo periods. That image is an open additive subgroup of the connected complex coordinate space, hence is the whole space. No evaluation separation, frame, primitive, local surjectivity or Jacobi inversion hypothesis remains in the original basis consumer.",
  "remaining": "Full real span and Jacobi inversion are proved. Discreteness of the actual integer period span and the principal-divisor kernel in both directions remain required for global complex Abel-Jacobi. Original torsion finiteness/cardinality and comparison back to Qbar divisor classes remain open, followed by Tate realization, rank-two Hecke/Frobenius and inertia comparison, arithmetic automorphy and higher symmetric-power continuation. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20. No acceptance gate closes here.",
  "production": "Scratch only; production promotion and verification pending.",
  "rootPinsChanged": false,
  "proofLimitsChanged": false
